      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2007 S. Karger AG, Basel.",
        "AbstractText": "Candida infection should be considered in an individual with a pelvic abscess that is unresponsive to conventional antibiotic therapy, particularly in the presence of an intrauterine device. We present a case of a tuboovarian abscess caused by Candida species in a woman with an intrauterine device for >10 years. Surgical intervention followed by antifungal therapy resulted in a favorable outcome."
      },
